doc:caseScholzAgVArmenia a echr:CaseDocument ;
    rdfs:label "Scholz AG v. Armenia"^^xsd:string ;
    echr:hasApplicant doc:partyScholzAg ;
    echr:hasApplicationNumber "16528/10"^^xsd:string ;
    echr:hasExtractionNote "No domestic proceedings are described in the provided facts prior to the ECHR application."^^xsd:string ;
    echr:hasJudgmentDate "2019-01-24"^^xsd:date ;
    echr:hasRespondentState "Republic of Armenia"^^xsd:string ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "**1.** The case originated in an application (no. 16528/10) against the Republic of Armenia lodged with the Court under Article 34 of the Convention for the Protection of Human Rights and Fundamental Freedoms (“the Convention”) by a German corporation, Scholz AG (“the applicant company”), on 19 March 2010."^^xsd:string .

doc:partyArmenianGovernment a echr:Party ;
    rdfs:label "The Armenian Government"^^xsd:string ;
    echr:hasPartyName "The Armenian Government"^^xsd:string ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "The Armenian Government (“the Government”) were represented by their Agent, Mr G. Kostanyan, Representative of the Government of Armenia to the European Court of Human Rights."^^xsd:string ;
    echr:isRepresentedBy doc:repGKostanyan .

doc:proceeding_cassation_decision_20090923 a echr:DomesticProceeding ;
    rdfs:label "Court of Cassation decision declaring appeal inadmissible (23 September 2009)"^^xsd:string ;
    echr:followsProceeding doc:proceeding_cassation_appeal_20090804 ;
    echr:hasCourt doc:domAuthCourtOfCassation ;
    echr:hasDecisionDate "2009-09-23"^^xsd:date ;
    echr:hasInstanceLevel echr:LevelCassation ;
    echr:hasOutcome echr:OutcomeDeclaredInadmissible ;
    echr:hasOutcomeDirection echr:DirectionUnfavourableToApplicant ;
    echr:hasParticipation doc:participation_llc_20090923,
        doc:participation_scholz_20090923 ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote """On 23 September 2009 the Court of Cassation declared the applicant company’s appeal on points of law inadmissible. In doing so, it stated the following:
“... As for the letter of the President of the Arbitration Tribunal of the Chamber of Commerce of 7 October 2008 concerning non-acceptance of the claim lodged by [the applicant company], it was based on the grounds that [the applicant company] had not submitted the original arbitration agreement or a certified copy, as required by the Commercial Arbitration Act and [the provisions contained therein], in the absence of which arbitration proceedings could not be started.
The Court of Cassation finds that, taking into account the failure to submit to the Arbitration Tribunal of the Chamber of Commerce and Industry the original arbitration agreement or a certified copy ... and non-examination of [the applicant company’s] claim, [the applicant company] is not deprived of judicial protection in accordance with the general provisions of the Code of Civil Procedure ...”"""^^xsd:string .

doc:proceeding_commercial_20070115 a echr:DomesticProceeding ;
    rdfs:label "Claim with the Commercial Court (15 January 2007)"^^xsd:string ;
    echr:hasCourt doc:domAuthCommercialCourt ;
    echr:hasParticipation doc:participation_llc_20070115,
        doc:participation_scholz_20070115 ;
    echr:hasProceedingStartDate "2007-01-15"^^xsd:date ;
    echr:hasProceedingType echr:TypeCivil ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "**14.** On 15 January 2007 the applicant company lodged a claim with the Commercial Court against the LLC, seeking to recover USD 10,000 from the initial debt of USD 1,213,824."^^xsd:string,
        "**15.** On 2 October 2007 the applicant company amended its initial claim, seeking to recover a total of USD 1,516,442 and EUR 116,600 from the LLC, including the principal debt, the loan and interest on both. It also requested a waiver of the court fees."^^xsd:string,
        "**16.** On 4 October 2007 the LLC filed a counterclaim, contesting the applicant company’s claims. The director of the LLC requested the annulment of the two documents dated 28 October 2005, arguing that, having no command of German, he had been unaware of their content and had signed them as a result of fraud."^^xsd:string,
        "**17.** On 15 October 2007 the applicant filed a response to the counterclaim, arguing, inter alia, that the director of the LLC had been personally present during the negotiations in Germany when a recalculation of liabilities between the companies had been carried out."^^xsd:string,
        "**18.** On 7 November 2007 the LLC requested the Commercial Court to leave the applicant company’s claim unexamined on the grounds that the contracts of 8 February 1999, 10 April 2000 and 2 April 2003 contained a dispute resolution clause whereby disputes concerning their performance would be resolved by the Arbitration Tribunal of the Chamber of Commerce of the country of the respondent"^^xsd:string .

doc:proceeding_commercial_appeal_20071123 a echr:DomesticProceeding ;
    rdfs:label "Appeal to three-judge bench of the Commercial Court (lodged 23 November 2007; decision 10 December 2007)"^^xsd:string ;
    echr:followsProceeding doc:proceeding_commercial_leave_unexamined_20071116 ;
    echr:hasCourt doc:domAuthCommercialCourt ;
    echr:hasDecisionDate "2007-12-10"^^xsd:date ;
    echr:hasInstanceLevel echr:LevelAppeal ;
    echr:hasParticipation doc:participation_llc_20071123,
        doc:participation_scholz_20071123 ;
    echr:hasProceedingStartDate "2007-11-23"^^xsd:date ;
    echr:hasProceedingType echr:TypeCivil ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "**20.** On 23 November 2007 the applicant company lodged a complaint concerning the decision to leave the claim and counterclaim unexamined. It argued, inter alia, that the agreements signed on 28 October 2005, which had succeeded the contracts of 8 February 1999, 10 April 2000 and 2 April 2003, provided that disputes concerning the failure of the LLC to respect the repayment schedules set out in them would be determined by the courts."^^xsd:string,
        "**21.** On 10 December 2007 a three-judge bench of the Commercial Court rejected the complaint submitted by the applicant company. The decision stated that, inter alia , the claims concerning the debt and the loan were interconnected and stemmed from the commercial relationships between the parties based on the contract for the supply of scrap metal."^^xsd:string .

doc:admin_arbitration_refusal_20081007 a echr:AdministrativeAction ;
    rdfs:label "Arbitration Tribunal refusal to start proceedings (7 October 2008)"^^xsd:string ;
    echr:followsProceeding doc:proceeding_arbitration_claim_20080917 ;
    echr:hasCourt doc:domAuthArbitrationTribunal ;
    echr:hasDecisionDate "2008-10-07"^^xsd:date ;
    echr:hasOutcome echr:OutcomeRefusedExamination ;
    echr:hasOutcomeDirection echr:DirectionUnfavourableToApplicant ;
    echr:hasParticipation doc:participation_scholz_refusal_20081007,
        doc:participation_tribunal_refusal_20081007 ;
    echr:hasProceedingType echr:TypeAdministrative ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "**26.** On 7 October 2008 the President of the Arbitration Tribunal informed the applicant company that its request to start arbitration proceedings would not be granted. The relevant parts of the letter read as follows: “... The promissory note of 8 November 2002 and the agreement of 28 October 2005, on which your claim was based, do not contain an arbitration clause and, moreover, the parties have not concluded any agreement to submit the disputes arising out of the performance of the above-mentioned promissory note and the agreement to the permanent arbitration institution of the Chamber of Commerce and Industry of Armenia for determination. Consequently, in the absence of an arbitration agreement between the parties, the [Arbitration Tribunal] cannot start arbitration proceedings.”"^^xsd:string .

doc:admin_reply_arbitration_20080801 a echr:AdministrativeAction ;
    rdfs:label "Reply from President of the Arbitration Tribunal (1 August 2008)"^^xsd:string ;
    echr:followsProceeding doc:admin_request_arbitration_20080723 ;
    echr:hasCourt doc:domAuthArbitrationTribunal ;
    echr:hasParticipation doc:participation_tribunal_reply_20080801 ;
    echr:hasProceedingStartDate "2008-08-01"^^xsd:date ;
    echr:hasProceedingType echr:TypeAdministrative ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "**23.** On 1 August 2008 the President of the Arbitration Tribunal replied that the question of whether the arbitration clause stipulated in the contracts concluded between the parties was sufficient for it to accept the claim for examination could only be determined once the claim had been lodged."^^xsd:string .

doc:participation_arbitration_20080723 a echr:Participation ;
    rdfs:label "Arbitration Tribunal participation (request, 23 July 2008)"^^xsd:string ;
    echr:hasPartySide echr:SideResponding ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "**22.** On 23 July 2008 the applicant company’s representative sent a request for information to the President of the Arbitration Tribunal..."^^xsd:string ;
    echr:participatingParty doc:domAuthArbitrationTribunal .

doc:participation_llc_20070115 a echr:Participation ;
    rdfs:label "the LLC participation (Commercial Court, 15 January 2007)"^^xsd:string ;
    echr:hasPartySide echr:SideResponding ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "**16.** On 4 October 2007 the LLC filed a counterclaim, contesting the applicant company’s claims. The director of the LLC requested the annulment of the two documents dated 28 October 2005, arguing that, having no command of German, he had been unaware of their content and had signed them as a result of fraud."^^xsd:string ;
    echr:participatingParty doc:partyLlc .

doc:participation_llc_20071116 a echr:Participation ;
    rdfs:label "the LLC participation (Commercial Court decision, 16 November 2007)"^^xsd:string ;
    echr:hasPartySide echr:SideInitiating ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "**19.** On 16 November 2007 the Commercial Court granted the request and decided to leave the applicant company’s claim and the counterclaim lodged by the LLC unexamined."^^xsd:string ;
    echr:participatingParty doc:partyLlc .

doc:participation_llc_20071123 a echr:Participation ;
    rdfs:label "the LLC participation (Commercial Court appeal, decision 10 December 2007)"^^xsd:string ;
    echr:hasPartySide echr:SideResponding ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "**21.** On 10 December 2007 a three-judge bench of the Commercial Court rejected the complaint submitted by the applicant company. The decision stated that, inter alia , the claims concerning the debt and the loan were interconnected and stemmed from the commercial relationships between the parties based on the contract for the supply of scrap metal."^^xsd:string ;
    echr:participatingParty doc:partyLlc .

doc:participation_llc_20080917 a echr:Participation ;
    rdfs:label "the LLC participation (Arbitration Tribunal claim, 17 September 2008)"^^xsd:string ;
    echr:hasPartySide echr:SideResponding ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "**25.** On 17 September 2008 the applicant company lodged a claim with the Arbitration Tribunal, seeking to recover EUR 116,600, the amount of the loan and interest."^^xsd:string ;
    echr:participatingParty doc:partyLlc .

doc:participation_llc_20081017 a echr:Participation ;
    rdfs:label "the LLC participation (Yerevan Civil Court claim, 17 October 2008)"^^xsd:string ;
    echr:hasPartySide echr:SideResponding ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "**27.** In view of the fact that the Commercial Court had been abolished by that time, on 17 October 2008 the applicant company lodged a claim with the Yerevan Civil Court, seeking to recover EUR 116,600 from the LLC, representing the amount of the loan and interest."^^xsd:string ;
    echr:participatingParty doc:partyLlc .

doc:participation_llc_20090313 a echr:Participation ;
    rdfs:label "the LLC participation (District Court, 13 March 2009)"^^xsd:string ;
    echr:hasPartySide echr:SideResponding ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "On 13 March 2009 the District Court accepted the case for examination."^^xsd:string ;
    echr:participatingParty doc:partyLlc .

doc:participation_llc_20090616 a echr:Participation ;
    rdfs:label "the LLC participation (request to leave unexamined, 12–16 June 2009)"^^xsd:string ;
    echr:hasPartySide echr:SideInitiating ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "On 12 June 2009 the LLC, relying on the decision of the Commercial Court of 16 November 2007, requested the District Court to leave the applicant company’s claim unexamined. It submitted, in particular, that the applicant company had failed to substantiate that the grounds for leaving its claim unexamined no longer existed."^^xsd:string ;
    echr:participatingParty doc:partyLlc .

doc:participation_llc_20090625 a echr:Participation ;
    rdfs:label "the LLC participation (reply to appeal, June 2009)"^^xsd:string ;
    echr:hasPartySide echr:SideResponding ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "In its reply to the applicant company’s appeal, the LLC submitted, inter alia, that the applicant company had failed to provide the Arbitration Tribunal with copies of the relevant extracts of the contracts that contained the arbitration clause and the relevant decisions of the Commercial Court. Therefore, the tribunal had refused to accept the claim."^^xsd:string ;
    echr:participatingParty doc:partyLlc .

doc:participation_llc_20090721 a echr:Participation ;
    rdfs:label "the LLC participation (Civil Court of Appeal decision, 21 July 2009)"^^xsd:string ;
    echr:hasPartySide echr:SideResponding ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote "On 21 July 2009 the Civil Court of Appeal upheld the decision of 16 June 2009. In doing so, it stated, in particular, that the applicant company had failed to submit to the Arbitration Tribunal extracts of the contracts containing the arbitration clause, as a result of which its claim had not been accepted."^^xsd:string ;
    echr:participatingParty doc:partyLlc .

doc:participation_llc_20090923 a echr:Participation ;
    rdfs:label "the LLC participation (Court of Cassation decision, 23 September 2009)"^^xsd:string ;
    echr:hasPartySide echr:SideResponding ;
    echr:hasSupportingQuote """On 23 September 2009 the Court of Cassation declared the applicant company’s appeal on points of law inadmissible. In doing so, it stated the following:
“... As for the letter of the President of the Arbitration Tribunal of the Chamber of Commerce of 7 October 2008 concerning non-acceptance of the claim lodged by [the applicant company], it was based on the grounds that [the applicant company] had not submitted the original arbitration agreement or a certified copy, as required by the Commercial Arbitration Act and [the provisions contained therein], in the absence of which arbitration proceedings could not be started.
The Court of Cassation finds that, taking into account the failure to submit to the Arbitration Tribunal of the Chamber of Commerce and Industry the original arbitration agreement or a certified copy ... and non-examination of [the applicant company’s] claim, [the applicant company] is not deprived of judicial protection in accordance with the general provisions of the Code of Civil Procedure ...”"""^^xsd:string ;
    echr:participatingParty doc:partyLlc .

